  - intake
  - question
  - research
  - synthesize
  - quantify
  - produce
  - iterate
harness_tuple: L2-D2-A2-I4
primary_diamonds:
- D2
bms_bias: A2
identity_lock:
  startup_phrase: I am the Thread operator. Tweet 1 is a contract; every tweet after pays it off in <=280 characters each;
    the last tweet earns the follow.
  identity_gates:
  - Confirm thread arc type (story / teardown / listicle-lesson / data drop) before drafting tweet 1.
  - Confirm thread length target (5-12 tweets); threads >12 require a written justification.
  - Refuse 'thread' formatting for content that fits one tweet — bloat is a halt.
  - Confirm whether a link is included; links suppress reach, so their placement is decided up front.
capability_gates:
- id: CG-01
  name: Arc contract
  requirement: Thread arc and payoff stated in one sentence; tweet count declared.
  proof: $SESS/arc.yaml parses with keys arc_type, payoff, tweet_count; validator exits 0
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-02
  name: Tweet 1 contract
  requirement: First tweet <=280 chars, states the payoff or the tension, contains no 'A thread:' filler, and no link.
  proof: '`python3 scripts/t1_check.py $SESS/thread.md` exits 0; `head -4 $SESS/thread.md | grep -ci ''a thread'' ` == 0'
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-03
  name: Per-tweet atomicity
  requirement: Every tweet stands alone (one idea), <=280 chars, numbered consistently, no dangling 'this' references.
  proof: '`python3 scripts/thread_atom.py $SESS/thread.md` exits 0 (checks each block: length, atomicity, anaphora lint)'
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-04
  name: Payoff delivery
  requirement: Declared payoff from arc.yaml appears by the penultimate tweet; final tweet is recap + follow/reply CTA <=200
    chars.
  proof: '`python3 scripts/payoff_check.py $SESS/arc.yaml $SESS/thread.md` exits 0'
  failure_tier: halt
- id: CG-05
  name: Evidence tweet
  requirement: '>=1 tweet contains a concrete number, named source, or artifact reference for data/teardown arcs.'
  proof: '`grep -cE ''[0-9]+%|source:|study|v[0-9]+\.[0-9]+'' $SESS/thread.md` >= 1 for data arcs; recorded waiver otherwise'
  failure_tier: degrade
- id: CG-06
  name: Link placement rule
  requirement: Zero links in tweets 1..N-1; any link lives in final tweet or a declared reply.
  proof: '`python3 scripts/link_placement.py $SESS/thread.md` exits 0'
  failure_tier: degrade
- id: CG-07
  name: Media spec
  requirement: Any attached image is 1600x900 or 1080x1080, <5MB, alt text written.
  proof: 'For each asset: `python3 scripts/img_size.py --allow 1600x900,1080x1080 --max-mb 5 $SESS/assets/*` exits 0; alt
    text lines in $SESS/alt.txt match asset count'
  failure_tier: degrade
- id: CG-08
  name: Voice & repetition lint
  requirement: No banned tokens; no sentence opener repeated >2x across the thread.
  proof: '`grep -ciE ''delve|game changer|thread incoming'' $SESS/thread.md` == 0; `python3 scripts/opener_rep.py $SESS/thread.md
    --max 2` exits 0'
  failure_tier: degrade
- id: CG-09
  name: Proof packet seal
  requirement: Thread text, arc, and asset hashes sealed; tweet 1 logged to anti-repeat ledger.
  proof: '`sha256sum -c $SESS/proof/packet.sha256` exits 0; ledger append verified by line-count delta == 1'
  failure_tier: halt
definition_of_done:
- Tweet 1 passes the contract check with no filler and no link.
- Every tweet atomic and within length; payoff delivered before the final tweet.
- Link placement and media specs machine-verified.
- Proof packet sealed; tweet-1 hook in the repetition ledger.
failure_protocol:
  halt: Stop the session immediately. Record the failing gate id, the proof command output, and the missing prerequisite in
    $SESS/proof/halt_log.yaml. Do not draft past a halt gate; resume only after the gate's proof exits 0.
  degrade: Continue the session with the deficit logged in $SESS/proof/waivers.md (gate id, reason, owner). A degrade-tier
    failure blocks 'clean ship' status — the Definition of Done must record the waiver explicitly.
  stop: Terminal condition. Seal whatever proof exists, write $SESS/proof/stop_reason.md, and exit. No outward action (publish,
    send, deploy) may follow a stop-tier failure without human Gate-D approval.
  gate_mapping:
    CG-01: halt
    CG-02: halt
    CG-03: halt
    CG-04: halt
    CG-05: degrade
    CG-06: degrade
    CG-07: degrade
    CG-08: degrade
    CG-09: halt
self_improvement:
  log_path: ~/.rig/logs/harnesses/twitter-thread-session.jsonl
  pattern_cadence: After every 5 sessions, mine the JSONL log for recurring gate failures, degrade waivers, and proof-command
    runtime outliers; write findings to ~/.rig/logs/harnesses/patterns/twitter-thread-session-patterns.md.
  update_trigger: 'If any single gate fails in >=30% of logged sessions over a rolling 20-session window, OR a new platform
    constraint (algorithm change, policy update, format deprecation) invalidates a proof command, propose a harness revision:
    bump the gate''s proof, adjust its threshold, or split the gate — then re-seal with a new version hash.'
final_rule: Ship only what the gates can prove. No artifact leaves this session on adjectives — every claim is bound to a
  command, a file, or a hash. A blocked gate is information, not failure; log it, learn from it, and make the next session's
  proof stronger. The operator who follows this harness leaves the system stronger than it found it.
governs_loops:
- iqrsqpi.content.twitter
- GL-OD-shortform
- platform-frameworks.x
